@startuml Kiwi_Qualification_Gates
!theme plain
skinparam backgroundColor white
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName "Latin Modern Roman"
skinparam defaultFontSize 13
skinparam ArrowColor #216875
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam nodesep 20
skinparam ranksep 24
title Proposed experimental progression: no gate claimed complete
top to bottom direction
rectangle "K0 / offline tooling\nknown bytes + conversion\n+ gap detection" as K0
rectangle "K1 / one receiver\nfull capture + guards\n+ TX confirmation" as K1
rectangle "K2 / pilot\n10 bursts per level\nup to 3 observers" as K2
rectangle "K3 / replication\n3 distinct session blocks\npath / UTC strata" as K3
rectangle "K4 / replay comparison\nfrozen holdout captures\npaired gains / losses" as K4
rectangle "K5 / optional diagnostic\nsingle-variable matrix\nseparate claim scope" as K5
K0 -right-> K1 : station rehearsal\n+ receiver readiness
K1 -right-> K2 : valid capture
K2 -down-> K3 : complete outcomes
K2 --> K4 : freeze corpus
K3 -left-> K4 : expanded holdout
K2 -right-> K5 : separate readiness
note bottom of K4
A failed decode may be valid
experiment evidence.
No progression here establishes an
operational bidirectional link.
No worldwide reliability target is
inferred from pilot recovery.
end note
@enduml
